{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01266",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.61,
      "end_seconds": 4.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.69,
      "end_seconds": 8.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.27,
      "end_seconds": 24.15,
      "duration_seconds": 13.88,
      "text": "Honestly, it's cramps in my calves at night, and my family pushed me to come. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.6,
      "end_seconds": 28.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "how many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.58,
      "end_seconds": 32.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "For nearly five years, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.55,
      "end_seconds": 42.44,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.15,
      "end_seconds": 63.85,
      "duration_seconds": 18.7,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say. Only stretching and walking about, and it's not much. I've had tingling in my feet too, for about a year. With tingling in my feet, it feels mild to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.11,
      "end_seconds": 71.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Have you had cramps in your calves at night before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.97,
      "end_seconds": 78.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last year it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.25,
      "end_seconds": 83.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.45,
      "end_seconds": 95.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.9,
      "end_seconds": 115.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 82, BP is 121 over 68, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.95,
      "end_seconds": 118.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.0,
      "end_seconds": 124.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.48,
      "end_seconds": 130.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.05,
      "end_seconds": 133.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.77,
      "end_seconds": 148.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Both calves are soft and not tender, and the pulses at your feet are good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.59,
      "end_seconds": 156.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.54,
      "end_seconds": 177.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Did you get swelling of the legs, chest pain or back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.85,
      "end_seconds": 184.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "no, uh, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.73,
      "end_seconds": 186.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "What about shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.64,
      "end_seconds": 190.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No. No shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.86,
      "end_seconds": 194.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.1,
      "end_seconds": 198.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Nothing there, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.21,
      "end_seconds": 218.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "So, have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.09,
      "end_seconds": 225.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Yes, I had a varicose vein procedure, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.18,
      "end_seconds": 232.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.01,
      "end_seconds": 238.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.7,
      "end_seconds": 249.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.98,
      "text": "right, so high blood pressure is already on your record we'll keep that in mind today is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.65,
      "end_seconds": 256.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.11,
      "end_seconds": 259.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.27,
      "end_seconds": 265.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.99,
      "end_seconds": 268.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.07,
      "end_seconds": 272.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.56,
      "end_seconds": 278.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.85,
      "end_seconds": 284.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.95,
      "end_seconds": 307.46,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause. Another possibility is a side effect of a medicine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.5,
      "end_seconds": 312.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.86,
      "end_seconds": 329.52,
      "duration_seconds": 16.66,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause, but I'd like to confirm we should do blood tests for muscle cramps let's book a vitamin level to look into tingling feet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.61,
      "end_seconds": 335.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.92,
      "end_seconds": 352.66,
      "duration_seconds": 15.74,
      "text": "Keep well hydrated through the day. One warning sign to remember: one leg becomes red, hot or swollen. In that case don't wait. Let's review you in four weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.93,
      "end_seconds": 356.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.05,
      "end_seconds": 358.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "take care now"
    }
  ]
}